//! The gallery harness (ui doc §11.2): a mini-launch loads `Modules/Common.lua`,
//! `Data/Global.lua` and `Modules/Main.lua` (methods only), then runs `lua/gallery/<name>.lua`;
//! the Rust counterpart `src/gallery/<name>.rs` builds the same controls through pob-ui-core.
//! Owner: U8. The module list is generated by build.rs from `src/gallery/*.rs`.
//!
//! # Writing a gallery (widget units, ui doc §11.3)
//!
//! A gallery `<name>` (by convention `<unit>_<what>`, e.g. `u9_button`) is three files, all owned
//! by the unit that writes them; nothing shared needs an edit:
//!
//! * `lua/gallery/<name>.lua` returns a table `G` with an optional `G:Init()` and a required
//!   `G:OnFrame(inputEvents, viewPort)`. It runs after `lua/gallery_launch.lua` (the mini-launch:
//!   PoB's class system, `colorCodes`, `main`'s methods and the `main:Init` option defaults) and
//!   typically builds a ControlHost from PoB classes and calls
//!   `host:ProcessControlsInput(inputEvents, viewPort)` and `host:DrawControls(viewPort)`.
//!   `inputEvents` is `main.inputEvents`, wiped after each frame.
//! * `src/gallery/<name>.rs` defines `pub fn app(parts: pob_host::PlatformParts) ->
//!   Box<dyn pob_host::App>`: the same controls through pob-ui-core (owning `parts.sg` and
//!   `parts.sys`, typically inside a `Cx`). `on_key_down`/`on_key_up`/`on_char` append to the
//!   input events; `on_frame` does what the Lua `OnFrame` does, then wipes them.
//! * Optionally `lua/gallery/<name>.pobscript`: the interactions (`.pobscript`, see
//!   `crate::runner`); without it the gallery runs `frames 3`.
//!
//! `tests/parity.rs` runs every gallery at 1280×800 @1.0 and 1920×1080 @1.5 and requires zero T3
//! divergences. A file `src/gallery/_<x>.rs` is a support module shared by galleries, not a gallery.

include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/galleries.rs"));
